    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-02T15:55:02+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-02T15:55:02+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-02T05:25:02Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-02T05:25:02Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system centred over southwestern NSW will continue to move eastwards and a high pressure system in the Bight to slowly drift eastwards. The high weakens on Tuesday allowing a cold front to move over the south of the state on Wednesday. Another ridge of high pressure follows on Thursday, with another cold front clipping the southeast on Friday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW015" description="Mount Lofty Ranges" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-02T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-03T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-02T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-02T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly clear. Slight chance of a shower near the Barossa Valley early this evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h decreasing to 15 to 20 km/h in the evening.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-03T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-04T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-02T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-03T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">The chance of fog in the early morning. Mostly sunny day. Light winds becoming west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the early afternoon then becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 4:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-04T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-05T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-03T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-04T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and early afternoon. Winds northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h turning southwesterly 30 to 45 km/h in the late morning then decreasing to 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 18 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-05T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-06T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-04T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-05T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-06T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-07T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-05T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-06T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog. Medium chance of showers in the south, slight chance elsewhere. Winds northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h shifting south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 10 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
